Subject: [PATCH 08544/11362] arc: witness silent
 candidate-router/frame-change-scorer degradation (Gaps finding 3)

REQ-ARC-WMTE-6230, 2026-08-08 adversarial live-agent review. Both loaders degraded
to None through bare `except Exception` with no counter, no stderr line, and no
witness field, even though SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG declares both components
enabled -- so a row could carry llm_on_row_valid: true while running fully
UNROUTED or with the action-effect prior silently inert.

Both loaders now populate a per-call diagnostic dict on a thread-local side
channel (`_component_load_diagnostics`, one slot per thread -- the scored swarm
runs one thread per game, so a plain module-level dict would let concurrently-
constructing games' diagnostics cross-contaminate) and print one greppable line
on every fallback or failure. E3AgentPolicy.__init__ reads its own thread's slot
immediately after each call; generator_liveness_witness() surfaces both
diagnostics unconditionally.

Neither loader's return type changed (still bare Any | None). A first attempt
changed both to return tuple[Any | None, dict]; a repo-wide grep found 10+ other
callers -- experiments, tests, and the production module
arc_reactive_verifier_filter.py -- depending on the old bare shape, so that
attempt was reverted in favour of this side channel.

Tests: tests/python/test_arc_component_load_diagnostics_20260808.py (19 tests),
including a thread-local isolation class. Regression sweep: the new file plus
this session's other Gaps-fix test files (57 tests), the competition-agent
adapter/gateway/liveness-lint/reactive-verifier-filter suites (71 tests), the
two other generator_liveness_witness-dependent suites (45 tests), and all 47
test files constructing E3AgentPolicy (424 tests, 5 pre-existing failures
confirmed via git-stash to reproduce identically against clean HEAD -- 2 already
filed, 3 newly discovered and filed in this commit) -- all green modulo those
pre-existing, unrelated failures.

Freshness-lint: 11 artifacts + one second-order cascade (an artifact citing two
of those 11 by content hash) acknowledged as verified-inert -- new code is
confined to E3AgentPolicy construction/introspection paths none of those
artifacts' scripts reach.

